        "observation": "Viewed the entire 640-by-1024 PNG once, including both labelled panels, their rightmost plot borders, x-axis arrows and bottommost plot borders. Both panels have square grid cells with two cells per coordinate unit. In (a) the solid rising boundary crosses the origin; dashed reading guides locate (-2,-1) and (2,1). Fine hatching occupies the half-plane above this line, including the upper-left area, while the lower-right area is clear. In (b) the solid steeper rising line crosses the y-axis at -1, the x-axis at 1/2 and the guide point (1,1). Fine hatching occupies its lower/right side, including the positive x-axis to the right of 1/2. Dashed horizontal guides are coordinate-reading aids, not region boundaries."
