        "observation": "Viewed the entire 640-by-1024 PNG once, including both labelled panels, the complete circle and its lower arc, both rightmost plot borders and the bottom-left hatched wedge. Grid calibration is two small squares per coordinate unit. In (a) the solid circle is centred at (0,0) and reaches x=+/-2 and y=+/-2; two solid vertical chords lie at x=-1 and x=1. Hatching fills both caps inside the circle outside those chords. The central strip and all area outside the circle are clear. In (b) two solid diagonals meet at (0,1); the rising line crosses (-1,0) and the falling line crosses (1,0). Only the left-facing wedge between these lines is hatched. Its upper boundary is the falling line and its lower boundary is the rising line; the corresponding right-facing wedge and the top and bottom sectors are clear."
