  "boundary_reading": "The actual region boundaries are solid, so the described point sets include these boundaries. Dashed coordinate guides in fig-26 are not inequalities. No finite plot-frame limits are mathematical givens: the half-planes and wedge continue beyond the drawing window.",
  "source_solutions": [
    {
      "source_number": "177",
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel": "a",
          "task": "Determine one complete inequality describing the hatched half-plane.",
          "derivation": "The line passes through (-2,-1), (0,0) and (2,1). Its slope is (1-0)/(2-0)=1/2 and its intercept is 0. The hatched point (0,1) lies above it. The boundary is solid.",
          "solution": "y >= x/2, equivalently 2y >= x.",
          "distinction": "Read the slope from the coordinate scale, select the upper half-plane and include the boundary."
        },
        {
          "panel": "b",
          "task": "Determine one complete inequality describing the hatched half-plane.",
          "derivation": "The line passes through (0,-1) and (1,1). Its slope is (1-(-1))/(1-0)=2 and its intercept is -1, so y=2x-1. The hatched point (1,0) satisfies 0<1 and is below the line. The boundary is solid.",
          "solution": "y <= 2x-1, equivalently 2x-y >= 1.",
          "distinction": "Retain the negative intercept, use the two-unit rise and identify the lower/right half-plane."
        }
      ],
      "full_task_loss_in_choice": "Selection can test recognition of the complete inequalities but cannot establish unaided production of their equations and inequality notation."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "186",
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel": "a",
          "task": "Describe both hatched circular caps as one complete point set using simultaneous inequalities.",
          "derivation": "The centred radius-2 circle gives x^2+y^2<=4. Hatching is inside the circle and on either outer side of the chords: x<=-1 OR x>=1. This alternative condition is equivalent over real coordinates to x^2>=1. Thus intersect the disk with the union of the two outer half-planes. Boundary chords and circular arcs are solid.",
          "solution": "x^2+y^2 <= 4 AND x^2 >= 1. Equivalently, the union of {x^2+y^2<=4, x<=-1} and {x^2+y^2<=4, x>=1}.",
          "distinction": "Combine disk intersection with cap union; x<=-1 AND x>=1 would be empty and the central strip is not hatched."
        },
        {
          "panel": "b",
          "task": "Describe the complete left-facing hatched wedge using a two-inequality system.",
          "derivation": "The rising boundary through (-1,0) and (0,1) is y=x+1. The falling boundary through (1,0) and (0,1) is y=1-x. In the hatched left wedge a point is above the rising line and below the falling line. Both inequalities hold simultaneously, and x+1<=1-x implies x<=0; (1,1) is in the opposite unhatched wedge. Both lines are solid.",
          "solution": "y >= x+1 AND y <= 1-x, equivalently x+1 <= y <= 1-x.",
          "distinction": "Preserve the two-line intersection and distinguish the left wedge from the right wedge and from the upper and lower sectors."
        }
      ],
      "full_task_loss_in_choice": "Selection can test recognition of complete point-set systems but cannot establish unaided production of the systems or unaided conversion of the two-cap union to a compound condition."
